{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1558613211,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDIzNjIyMzE2ODI="},"added":["UX"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1558615319,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ5NTIwMjA5MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3450#issuecomment-495202091"},"message":"I don't have an idea how we could improve upon that besides doing initial sensing if we can login (I thought we actually did) and giving error even without trying to run git.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1570879138,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU0MTMxNTMyMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3450#issuecomment-541315322"},"message":"Here is how to replicate this issue:\n\n```\n/tmp % datalad create lcl\n/tmp % mkdir bareremote\n/tmp % git -C bareremote init --bare\n/tmp % cd lcl\n% datalad siblings add -s bareremote --url datalad-test:/tmp/bareremote\n% datalad publish --to bareremote --transfer-data all\nmih@datalad-test: Permission denied (publickey,password).\n[WARNING] Failed to run cmd ['ssh', '-fN', '-o', 'ControlMaster=auto', '-o', 'ControlPersist=15m', '-o', 'ControlPath=/home/mih/.cache/datalad/sockets/c5820c82', 'datalad-test']. Exit code=255\n| stdout: None\n| stderr: None \n[ERROR  ] Cmd('/usr/lib/git-annex.linux/git') failed due to: exit code(128)\n|   cmdline: /usr/lib/git-annex.linux/git fetch --progress -v bareremote\n|   stderr: 'fatal: Could not read from remote repository.\n| \n| Please make sure you have the correct access rights\n| and the repository exists.' [cmd.py:wait:412] (GitCommandError) \n```\n\nwith:\n\n```\n% grep datalad-test /etc/hosts\n127.0.0.1       datalad-test\n% grep -A1 datalad-test ~/.ssh/config\nHost datalad-test\n  PreferredAuthentications publickey\n```\n\nand no private key listed in `~/.ssh/authorized_keys`","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1570882694,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU0MTMxOTYxNA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3450#issuecomment-541319614"},"message":"Looking into this I cannot agree with @yarikoptic's assessment. Here is why:\n\n1. `GitRepo._call_gitpy_with_progress()` does not eval `SSHConnection.open()`\n  It returns a bool (or `None`) to indicates connection open success. This return value is ignored and datalad proceeds leading to the ultimate `error`. On failure, an early abort is possible.\n\n2. `SSHConnection.open()` should not issue a warning.\n  This method clearly documents if things worked out in its return value. There is no way for it to figure out, whether the caller has plans to deal with an error, and no way to disable the prominent warning in this case. In the spirit of https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1769 it should relay all relevant information to the caller.\n\nI propose to: RF `SSHConnection.open()` to:\n   - return `True` on success, `False` on an already open connection (although I am not sure when this could be relevant)\n   - raise `CommandError` when things go wrong in any way\n\nATM it is not meaningful to RF `GitRepo._call_gitpy_with_progress()`. With the above change, processing will stop before leading to subsequent errors (improves the status quo). There is no way to introduce meaningful result generation, because all its callers (`fetch`, `push`, `pull`) directly and immediately return internal GitPy data structures. Once this practice is discontinued, proper errors can be generated that feed into the result reporting infrastructure.","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1570882694,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDI5MTk4OTI2NA=="},"target":"fd5fb895e5ad55fbeadf3e856f81932b5f30be3ee6acd277156c45757f231b9a","message":"Looking into this I cannot agree with @yarikoptic's assessment. Here is why:\n\n1. `GitRepo._call_gitpy_with_progress()` does not eval `SSHConnection.open()`\n  It returns a bool (or `None`) to indicates connection open success. This return value is ignored and datalad proceeds leading to the ultimate `error`. On failure, an early abort is possible.\n\n2. `SSHConnection.open()` should not issue a warning.\n  This method clearly documents if things worked out in its return value. There is no way for it to figure out, whether the caller has plans to deal with an error, and no way to disable the prominent warning in this case. In the spirit of https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1769 it should relay all relevant information to the caller.\n\nI will RF `SSHConnection.open()` to:\n   - return `True` on success, `False` on an already open connection (although I am not sure when this could be relevant)\n   - raise `CommandError` when things go wrong in any way\n\nATM it is not meaningful to RF `GitRepo._call_gitpy_with_progress()`. With the above change, processing will stop before leading to subsequent errors (improves the status quo). There is no way to introduce meaningful result generation, because all its callers (`fetch`, `push`, `pull`) directly and immediately return internal GitPy data structures. Once this practice is discontinued, proper errors can be generated that feed into the result reporting infrastructure.","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1570884371,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDI3MDgwNjQ3OTQ="},"added":["fix-implemented"],"removed":[]},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1571029161,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MjcwOTIyMTg3OQ=="},"status":2}]}